CAT = "s24Comms"; SEG = "COM"
Q = [
('An email a representative sends to 18 retail customers within 30 days is correspondence. Under Rule 2210 it:',
 'Needs no principal approval before use but must be reviewed under the firm\'s procedures', ['Must be approved by a principal before it is sent', 'Must be filed with FINRA within 10 business days', 'Needs the CEO\'s signature before it is sent'],
 'Rule 2210(b)(2) subjects correspondence to the supervision and review requirements of Rules 3110(b) and 3110.06 to .09, which allow risk-based post-use review by a principal, rather than pre-use approval.'),
('A firm writes a brochure for its website describing its services to retail investors. Under Rule 2210 it generally needs:',
 'Approval by an appropriately qualified principal before first use', ['Review by FINRA staff before it is posted', 'Only a review after publication', 'No review, since it names no specific security'],
 'Rule 2210(b)(1) requires an appropriately qualified registered principal to approve each retail communication before the earlier of its use or filing with FINRA, subject to listed exceptions.'),
('A firm\'s presentation is distributed only to pension plans and insurance companies. Under Rule 2210 this institutional communication:',
 'Needs written review procedures but not prior principal approval', ['Must be filed with FINRA before use', 'Needs principal approval before first use', 'Is not subject to any FINRA standards'],
 'Rule 2210(b)(3) requires written procedures for reviewing institutional communications, but not pre-use principal approval. The content standards of Rule 2210(d) still apply, and it is treated as retail if the firm knows it will be passed on to retail investors.'),
('A representative posts a static message about the firm\'s new managed account program on a public social media profile. Under FINRA guidance this post is:',
 'A retail communication that needs principal approval before posting', ['Correspondence reviewed only after posting', 'An institutional communication', 'A public appearance not subject to review'],
 'FINRA guidance (Regulatory Notices 10-06 and 17-18) treats static content such as profiles and posted ads as retail communications needing pre-approval, while interactive real-time content is supervised like correspondence.'),
('A customer posts praise of a representative on a third-party site. The firm becomes responsible for that post as its own communication if it:',
 'Adopts or endorses the content, or helped prepare it', ['Simply allows the site to exist', 'Has a page on the same platform', 'Does not ask the site to remove it'],
 'Under FINRA guidance a third-party post is not the firm\'s communication unless the firm adopts or endorses it, or is entangled by being involved in preparing it.'),
('Under Rule 3230, a firm may make cold calls to residences only between:',
 '8 a.m. and 9 p.m. local time of the person called', ['9 a.m. and 5 p.m. local time of the firm', '7 a.m. and 10 p.m. local time of the person called', 'Any time on business days'],
 'Rule 3230 forbids outbound telephone solicitations to a residence before 8 a.m. or after 9 p.m. local time at the called person\'s location, unless the person consents or has an established business relationship.'),
('A person asks the firm to stop calling her. Under Rule 3230 the firm must honor that do-not-call request within a reasonable time that may not exceed:',
 '30 days', ['24 hours', '10 business days', '90 days'],
 'Rule 3230 requires a member to honor a firm-specific do-not-call request within a reasonable time, not to exceed 30 days, and to keep the request for five years.'),
('A firm may call a person who is on the national do-not-call registry if that person:',
 'Bought a security through the firm 12 months ago', ['Bought a car from a dealer in the same town', 'Visited the firm\'s website once a year ago', 'Is listed in a public phone directory'],
 'Rule 3230 excepts persons with an established business relationship, which includes a securities transaction or account with the firm within the preceding 18 months, or an inquiry within the preceding three months.'),
('Under Rule 3230, a firm that makes telemarketing calls must:',
 'Transmit caller ID showing its number or a number answered during business hours', ['Use only prerecorded messages for first calls', 'Read every caller\'s CRD number aloud', 'Record every call for six years'],
 'Rule 3230 requires members making telephone solicitations to transmit caller identification information, including a number that can be called during regular business hours to make a do-not-call request.'),
('A representative will speak at a public seminar and hand out printed slides. The slides are:',
 'Retail communications that need principal approval before use', ['Exempt, since the seminar is a public appearance', 'Institutional communications', 'Correspondence reviewed after the event'],
 'Under Rule 2210(f), scripts, slides, handouts and similar materials prepared for a public appearance are communications, and those given to retail investors need principal approval before use.'),
('When a firm keeps a record of a retail communication under Rule 2210, the record must include:',
 'The name of the principal who approved it and the date of approval', ['The home address of every person who saw it', 'FINRA\'s approval number for it', 'A copy of each customer\'s reply to it'],
 'Rule 2210(b)(4) requires members to keep communications for the period in SEC Rule 17a-4(b), including the name of the person who prepared each retail communication and the name of the principal who approved it, with the date.'),
('A representative uses a personal messaging app to discuss a client\'s trades because the firm cannot capture it. This is a problem because:',
 'Business communications must be captured and kept by the firm', ['Clients may not discuss trades by text at all', 'Only the CEO may use messaging apps', 'Messages must be reviewed by FINRA first'],
 'Exchange Act Rule 17a-4(b)(4) and FINRA Rules 3110 and 4511 require firms to keep and supervise business communications. Business messages on unapproved, uncaptured channels violate those requirements.'),
]
